From: vyos-mox <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: do not reboot through EFI ResetSystem() on the Turris Mox

U-Boot implements the EFI runtime ResetSystem() with a PSCI SYSTEM_RESET call,
which hangs the Armada 3720 once Linux has run. When booted via EFI the
generic arm64 machine_restart() calls it before any restart handler, so the
watchdog restart handler never runs. Skip efi_reboot() on cznic,turris-mox.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 #include <linux/hw_breakpoint.h>
 #include <linux/personality.h>
 #include <linux/notifier.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <trace/events/power.h>
 #include <linux/percpu.h>
 #include <linux/thread_info.h>
@@ -135,8 +136,14 @@
 	/*
 	 * UpdateCapsule() depends on the system being reset via
 	 * ResetSystem().
+	 *
+	 * Not on the Turris Mox: U-Boot implements the runtime ResetSystem()
+	 * with a PSCI SYSTEM_RESET call, which hangs the Armada 3720 once
+	 * Linux has run, whereas the watchdog restart handler resets the SoC
+	 * reliably. Do not let EFI pre-empt the restart handlers there.
 	 */
-	if (efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES))
+	if (efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES) &&
+	    !of_machine_is_compatible("cznic,turris-mox"))
 		efi_reboot(reboot_mode, NULL);
 
 	/* Now call the architecture specific reboot code. */
